024 - Kaiko - Research', content='Quarterly Report: Q4 2024 - Kaiko - Research Recap of 2024 as BTC Breaks $100K Read our Latest Report Insights Reports Analyst Calls Liquidity Ranking Contact Data+ Kaiko Data Insights Reports Analyst Calls Liquidity Ranking Contact Data+ Kaiko Data Digital Assets Market Data Scaled for Institutions Home Reports Quarterly Report: Q4 2024 Quarterly Market Report : Q4 2024 Expert analysis on the most significant crypto market events. Breaking Down Q4 with charts and data The final quarter of 2024 brought significant changes to the cryptocurrency market. In October, the U.S. SEC sued crypto market maker Cumberland DRIW, while Kraken launched its Layer 2 Ink on Optimism’s Superchain. November saw Bitcoin hit a new all-time high and Gary Gensler announce his resignation. December highlights included Bitcoin surpassing $100K, Coincheck going public, and the SEC approving the first spot BTC-ETH combo ETFs. Despite volatility, institutional interest in Bitcoin remained strong, with increased corporate holdings and the launch of spot Bitcoin ETF options. Bitcoin’s Post Election Rally Institutional Momentum Stays Strong Altcoin Markets Recovery Crypto Derivatives Signal Bullishness The Battle for Stablecoin Dominance Download the Report . Previous Quarterly Reports Quarterly Market Report 03/10/2024 Quarterly Report: Q3 2024 The past few months in financial markets have been punctuated by short periods of volatility. In August, crypto prices plunged as traders grappled with shifting macroeconomic conditions around the globe. Despite the intermittent volatility and the typical lower volumes over the summer months, there were some bright spots. Altcoins gained traction towards the end of the quarter as liquidity conditions improved. Meanwhile, BTC ETFs’ trade volumes and inflows remained robust amid market uncertainty and large liquidations. Download Quarterly Market Report 04/07/2024 Quarterly Report: Q2 2024 The past few months have been challenging, with Mt. Gox repayments putting pressure on the market and ETFs losing traction despite ETH ETF approvals. However, there were positive surprises, including filings for two spot SOL ETFs and a positive outlook for crypto in emerging markets like Turkey. Download Company About Contact - Research Contact - Data Compliance Careers Data Services Data Products API Docs Instrument Explorer Data Delivery Data Guides Research Insights Reports Analyst Calls Newsletters Our Analysts Contact 750 Lexington Ave New York, NY 10022 2 rue de Choiseul 75002 Paris – France Twitter – Linkedin Powered by Spin Interactive', timestamp=datetime.datetime(2025, 1, 11, 21, 41, 14, 902681), status='success', summary={'analysis_type': 'general', 'assets': [{'ticker': 'BTC', 'rating': 'Buy - Strong institutional interest and ETF approvals support long-term growth.', 'target_price': '$120,000 - $130,000', 'sentiment': 'Bullish', 'catalysts': ['Bitcoin surpassing $100K', 'SEC approval of spot BTC-ETH combo ETFs', 'Increased corporate holdings'], 'kpis': ['New all-time high in November', 'Strong ETF trade volumes and inflows'], 'action': 'Add Long', 'sources': ['Kaiko Quarterly Report Q4 2024', 'SEC filings', 'Institutional investment reports']}], 'sector': {'name': 'Cryptocurrency', 'sentiment': 'Bullish', 'catalysts': ['Launch of Bitcoin spot ETFs', 'Altcoin market recovery', 'Stablecoin dominance battle'], 'kpis': ['Increased liquidity in altcoin markets', 'Stablecoin market share metrics'], 'top_assets': ['BTC - All-time high and ETF approvals', 'ETH - Part of BTC-ETH combo ETFs', 'SOL - Potential new spot ETFs filings'], 'recommendation': 'Overweight', 'sources': ['Kaiko Quarterly Report Q4 2024', 'SEC announcements', 'Market liquidity reports']}, 'macro': {'indicators': ['Institutional investment trends', 'Regulatory changes (SEC actions)'], 'interest_rates': 'Stable with potential for rate cuts boosting risk assets', 'global_factors': 'Post-election economic policies and their impa